# ── Terminal app: LLM backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# OPTIONAL. Without a key the Terminal still works: unrecognized commands get an
# in-character canned reply instead of a real model response. Add a key to make
# the assistant live.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key. .env.local is gitignored —
# the key is read server-side only, in app/api/terminal/route.ts, and never
# reaches the browser.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model used by the terminal assistant. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001,
# which is fast and cheap — the right trade for one-line terminal replies.
# TERMINAL_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# ── WhisperFlow app: dictation backend ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# OPTIONAL, exactly like the key above. Without it WhisperFlow starts in DEMO
# MODE: it replays scripted transcripts instead of listening, so the app is
# fully explorable with no key, no microphone and no internet.
#
# With a key, WhisperFlow records from the microphone and transcribes for real.
# The audio is POSTed to /api/whisper on THIS server, and the server calls
# OpenAI — the browser never talks to openai.com directly. That is what keeps
# the site's "no cross-origin requests from the page" guarantee intact.
#
# Read server-side only, in app/api/whisper/route.ts. There is deliberately no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variant: a public key would be readable by every visitor.
#
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Transcription model. Defaults to whisper-1, which every OpenAI account has.
# WHISPER_MODEL=whisper-1
